        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "Managers use contribution margin to explore break-even volume, product mix, and the effect of changing price or variable cost. The result is only as good as the assumptions. Costs may change outside a relevant range, capacity may be limited, and demand may respond to price. Contribution margin is a decision model, not a substitute for context."
        },
