          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "Imagine a product sells for one hundred dollars and requires sixty dollars of variable cost for each unit. The forty-dollar difference is its unit contribution margin. It is not automatically profit. It is the amount that one additional sale contributes toward fixed costs and, after those are covered, operating profit."
